        "original_id": "3b535111-7661-5ddd-9c61-33f995b0239f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dick Crealy, Richard Crealy, Mary Pierce, Peaches Bartkowicz, Larisa Neiland\n- Events: 1970 Australian Open, 1970 Swedish Open, 2000 Sparkassen Cup – Doubles, Olympics\n- Organizations: Australian Davis Cup Team, Women's Tennis Association\n- Roles: former tennis player, retired tennis professional, defending champions\n- Topics: tennis, Grand Slam doubles\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Crealy was born on 18 September 1944 and is an Australian former tennis player.\n- In 1970, Richard Crealy reached the final of the Australian Open and was a member of the 1970 Australian Davis Cup Team.\n- In 1970, Dick Crealy and Peaches Bartkowicz won the singles titles at the 1970 Swedish Open.\n- Richard Crealy won four Grand Slam doubles titles.\n- Mary Pierce was born on 15 January 1975 and is a French retired tennis professional who played on the Women's Tennis Association tour.\n- Mary Pierce represented France in team competitions and at the Olympics.\n- Mary Pierce and Larisa Neiland were the defending champions for the 2000 Sparkassen Cup – Doubles, but neither competed that year.",
